\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{Behavior policies and executable-policy identity}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{provenance}

\p{Off-policy methods distinguish the
behavior and current policies, while language-model artifacts also depend on
tokenization and decoding. Section 3 of \citef{miao2026when} records the
behavior/current distinction. The additional artifact and implementation
fields in the proposed policy stamp make the executable law reproducible.}

\p{The stamp identifies an executable law; it does not claim that two
implementations with different stamps must behave differently on every task.}
